# Input graph for anuzzolese__pyrml__pyrml_pyrml_core.py__TripleMappings_from_rdf.
#
# from_rdf finds candidate triples-map subjects via a predicate-path
# (rml:logicalSource | rr:logicalTable), restricted to a specific subject
# only when `parent` resolves one via rr:parentTriplesMap, then keeps only
# those that carry rr:subjectMap. Two driver calls read this same graph
# (see driver.py):
#
#   * parent=None (subject wildcard): candidates are every triples map
#     reachable by EITHER predicate, anywhere -- ex:tmA (via
#     rml:logicalSource), ex:tmB (via rr:logicalTable) and ex:tmC (via
#     rml:logicalSource, also reachable through ex:refMap). ex:tmB has NO
#     rr:subjectMap -- the FALSE branch of the region's one true existence
#     check, `bool(m{ {tm} rr:subjectMap ?x })` -- so it must be excluded;
#     ex:tmA and ex:tmC both have one and must both be selected. Expected:
#     {ex:tmA, ex:tmC} (a two-element multiset -- ex:tmB is the
#     zero-solution/False proof, not a third member).
#   * parent=<http://example.org/refMap>: `tm` resolves via
#     rr:parentTriplesMap to ex:tmC, restricting the predicate-path read to
#     subject=ex:tmC alone. Expected: {ex:tmC} only -- ex:tmA (a different
#     subject) must NOT leak in even though it satisfies the same
#     predicate-path pattern; this is the neighbourhood proof that the
#     untranslated `g.triples((tm, path, None))` line still scopes
#     correctly once `tm` comes from the translated `.first()` read.
@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/> .
@prefix rr:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/r2rml#> .
@prefix rml: <http://semweb.mmlab.be/ns/rml#> .

# ex:tmA -- top-level triples map (via rml:logicalSource), HAS a
# rr:subjectMap -> selected whenever it is a candidate at all.
ex:tmA rml:logicalSource ex:src1 ;
    rr:subjectMap ex:sm1 .

# ex:tmB -- top-level triples map (via rr:logicalTable, the OTHER side of
# the alternation), but NO rr:subjectMap -> the zero-solution case.
ex:tmB rr:logicalTable ex:table1 .

# ex:refMap -- a referencing object map whose rr:parentTriplesMap points at
# ex:tmC.
ex:refMap rr:parentTriplesMap ex:tmC .

# ex:tmC -- reached both as a top-level candidate (parent=None) and as the
# resolved parent (parent=ex:refMap); has a subjectMap -> selected in both
# calls.
ex:tmC rml:logicalSource ex:src2 ;
    rr:subjectMap ex:sm2 .
